      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T02:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the experiment, we use flag\u003d0 for control group.\nAnd isFeatureEnabled returns default value if the flag\u003d0.\nSo, if we have the debuggable devices in control groups, we can not compare the metrics between control groups and treatment groups.\n\nTemplate we are using rollout the feature via teamfood, droidfood, beta, and public.\nDo we know how much debuggable devices we have in beta or public?\nIf we don\u0027t have many debuggable devices in beta or public stage, this is maybe fine since we don\u0027t have many devices in teamfood or droidfood and we can not compare the metrics in these stages.\n\n@xiaom@google.com, Do you check the metrics in teamfood or droidfood?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "663f0d12_54024d1f",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T03:53:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In the experiment, we use flag\u003d0 for control group.\n\nIs this a feature of how *we* run experiments, or how experiments generally work? How did this work when we passed in defaultEnabled \u003d isAtLeastU() (which was mostly true on droidfood)?",
      "parentUuid": "628545ea_292eddef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0f26ccc_435781a6",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T04:35:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is how we run experiment with our utils (isFeatureEnabled and isFeatureNotChickenedOut).\nFor feature we did `defaultEnabled \u003d isAtLeastU()`, we specify `base.Not(android_version.IsPlatformUAbove)` in PropagationCriteria.\nI\u0027m not sure if we can specify debuggable device in PropagationCriteria.",
      "parentUuid": "663f0d12_54024d1f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "226d10be_80f330ac",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-18T05:32:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could see some experiment configuration specifies that.\nIt seems we can push the flag only for non debuggable devices.\nIf we update the experiment to run only on non debuggable devices, this change should be fine.",
      "parentUuid": "f0f26ccc_435781a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70683ce5_6921ef46",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1406251
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T03:17:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do we know how much debuggable devices we have in beta or public?\n\nWe don\u0027t know the userdebug and eng builds in beta or public for now, but we should be able to query that from raw data table. Assume that we have this change, then the control group (default value is 0) will enable the feature on debuggable devices as well, not sure if that will bring the imbalance of device count between control and treatment groups. However, if there are not too many debuggable devices, then it should be fine.\n\n\u003e Do you check the metrics in teamfood or droidfood?\n\nYes, usually I check droidfood 50% for A/B before we can ramp up to public(e.g. we have to file an exception for public).\n\nBtw, think about this(maybe a different topic), do we have any way to enable the feature only on U and above with isFeatureNotChickenedOut()? So far the workflow of enabling a feature is:\n- use launch_through_droidfood_beta_and_public or to_public_mainline templates for experiment rollout, but these templates has only Pixel device restriction.\n- after experiment launch, we change the production code and call isFeatureNotChickenedOut to enable the feature on all platforms, and rollout the feature via binary push to OEMs\u0027 devices.\n\nWhat if we would like to enable the feature only on U and above devices? In this case, which API should we call in the production code?",
      "parentUuid": "226d10be_80f330ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5164be16_ab8f95e1",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T03:37:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  not sure if that will bring the imbalance of device count between control and treatment groups.\n\nMy concern was we can not easily compare the metrics between control group and treatment group on Rasta by this change.\nIt seems this could be solved by adding non-debuggable to the PropagationCriteria in study.\nIf we have many debuggable devices in droidfood, this change reduces the number of devices in droidfood and makes it difficult to compare the metrics.\nThough I\u0027m not sure metrics in droidfood is usefull since they already don\u0027t have many devices.\n\n\u003e What if we would like to enable the feature only on U and above devices? In this case, which API should we call in the production code?\n\nWe can have check in the caller side, I think.\nAlso we need to add isAtleastU to the PropagationCriteria of the study so that we can compare the metrics.\n```\nenabled \u003d isAtleastU() || isFeatureEnabled();\nof\nenabled \u003d isAtleastU() || isFeatureNotChickenedOut();\n```",
      "parentUuid": "70683ce5_6921ef46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1234f87e_70f8292f",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T03:41:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What if we would like to enable the feature only on U and above devices?\n\nUnfortunately, with trunk stable basing this off of SDK level may not work as expected. U has released, so it includes user devices. And FWIU, trunk stable droidfood is also running U (QPR2).",
      "parentUuid": "70683ce5_6921ef46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da904c2b_b58bb346",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T03:57:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s true.\nWe have some discussion with trunk stable team but we don\u0027t have a way to distinguish QPRs for now.\nPossibly we will be able to use aconfig flag for some situations.",
      "parentUuid": "1234f87e_70f8292f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f305e51_539ee23e",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T04:15:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIU, I think there are really three options:\n1) use force disable (-1) as a default in all experiments and continue with this change.\n2) Exclude debuggable build from all experiments using propagation experiment.\n3) Exclude debuggable builds from just the APF experiment and do something like Motomu suggests `isDebuggable() || isFeatureEnabled()`.\n\n\u003e If we have many debuggable devices in droidfood\n\nI would imagine the droidfood population to be almost exclusively debuggable builds (it requires dev-keys to participate). (Not sure if the build server provides dev-keys signed -user builds? Probably? Though that is probably not super helpful when droidfooding.)",
      "parentUuid": "1234f87e_70f8292f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23bbbf80_61e9a3a4",
        "filename": "staticlibs/device/com/android/net/module/util/DeviceConfigUtils.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T06:03:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I prefer solution3 since this change will be applied only to APF experiment and we don’t need to worry about other experiments.\nIf we really need a way to disable the feature on droidfood, I think we can use\n```\nenabled \u003d isDebuggable() ? isFeatureNotChickenedOut() : isFeatureEnabled().\n```\n\n\u003e 1) use force disable (-1) as a default in all experiments and continue with this change.\n\nThe process we currently follow to launch the feature is 1) run launch with isFeatureEnabled 2) replace isFeatureEnabled by isFeatureNotChickenedOut to rollout feature to OEM devices.\nIf we push -1 to devices as default at step1, we need to update the default value to 0 at step2.\nThis should be fine but I don’t want to change the behavior by default value change if we can avoid.\n\n\u003e 2) Exclude debuggable build from all experiments using propagation experiment.\n\nWith this change, we can not compare the metrics in droidfood.\nI’m not sure if this is fine for all the experiment.",
      "parentUuid": "2f305e51_539ee23e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 184,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "d5d38374f7a62cf6fb2ee362257cfbf1ba8d65b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
